{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Moses and Aaron came</b>. Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 10:3) wrote: We know that Moses would never come to Pharaoh without Aaron with him, for he is the interpreter, but now he mentioned \"Moses and Aaron\" because Pharaoh had commanded to bring back the two of them, after he had driven them out the last time — which he had not done in all the plagues."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:05:16.644724625Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}